    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:haggadah:magid/bechol_dor_vador">
        <tei:milestone unit="paragraph" n="1" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:haggadah:magid/bechol_dor_vador/1"/>
        <tei:p>In every generation one must view oneself as though one had personally left Egypt, as scripture instructs: “And you shall say to your child on that day, ‘This is because of what the Lord did for me when I left Egypt.’”[40] Exodus 13:8 It was not only our ancestors that the blessed Holy One redeemed. Rather, even we were redeemed with them, as scripture says: “And he brought us out of there in order to bring us to and give us the land that he promised to our ancestors.”[41] Deut 6:23</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
